; expect 42
; Trait dispatch is name RESOLUTION, so it obeys the same order as
; every other resolution in the checker: a frame-local binding first,
; then a declaration, and the trait only if neither claimed the
; spelling. Until 2026-08-10 it asked nothing at all - `traitRewrite`
; ran on the head of every application whose spelling a trait owned
; and mutated it to the implementation's mangled name - so declaring
; a trait method made that spelling globally unavailable.
;
; Each term below is a way that was wrong, and the sum discriminates:
;
;   a  a `let` binding of the method's name. Answered 111, the
;      implementation, where the language says 7;
;   b  a function PARAMETER of the method's name. Same 111, and this
;      is the term that separates "checks the scope" from "checks the
;      top level" - a parameter is in no declaration list;
;   c  an imported standard-library function of the method's name.
;      Answered `AX3025 no implementation of `Len` for `String``,
;      i.e. a valid program refused. The concrete definition wins;
;   d, e  nothing else claims `sz`, so dispatch still happens and
;      still picks by the ARGUMENT's type. These are the control: a
;      guard written too wide turns dispatch off and takes them with
;      it.
;
; The entry-file half of the same defect - a top-level `fn` whose
; name a trait already claimed, which answered 111 with no
; diagnostic - is `tests/diagnostics/445-trait-method-duplicate.ax`.
(import Str)

(trait (Sz a) where
  (sz :: (-> a Int)))

(impl (Sz Int) where
  ((sz (lambda (n) 111))))

(impl (Sz Bool) where
  ((sz (lambda (b) 222))))

; A trait whose method is spelled like the `Str` function above.
(trait (Len a) where
  (strLen :: (-> a Int)))

(impl (Len Bool) where
  ((strLen (lambda (b) 999))))

(:: viaParam (-> (-> Int Int) Int))
(fn (viaParam sz) (sz 5))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (let ((a (let ((sz (lambda (q) 7))) (sz 5))))
    (let ((b (viaParam (lambda (q) 7))))
      (let ((c (strLen "abcd")))
        (let ((d (sz 5)))
          (let ((e (sz true)))
            (if (== (+ (+ (+ (+ a b) c) d) e) 351) 42 1)))))))
